BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 8.00 Tf ET
BT /Ff5d2de5f3a71699ae4b2d83179e62d09e6fc4126 18.00 Tf ET
BT 56.69 779.53 Td (1 Introduction) Tj ET
BT /Ff5d2de5f3a71699ae4b2d83179e62d09e6fc4126 13.00 Tf ET
BT 56.69 745.51 Td (1.1 Database Systems and Their Tasks) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 722.83 Td (A database system consists of a database, the collection of stored data, and a database management) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 708.55 Td (system \(DBMS\), the software that manages it. Applications do not access files directly; they send) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 694.26 Td (requests to the DBMS, which takes care of storage, access paths, concurrency and recovery. This) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 679.98 Td (separation is what allows many users and programs to share the same data safely.) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 657.12 Td (Typical tasks of a DBMS are the integration of data into one consistent collection, operations to query) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 642.83 Td (and modify data, a catalog that describes the stored data, user views, integrity constraints, access) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 628.54 Td (control, transactions and recovery after failures. Together these tasks distinguish a database system) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 614.26 Td (from a set of files that each application manages on its own.) Tj ET
BT /Ff5d2de5f3a71699ae4b2d83179e62d09e6fc4126 13.00 Tf ET
BT 56.69 580.06 Td (1.2 The Three-Schema Architecture) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 557.38 Td (The ANSI/SPARC architecture describes a database on three levels. The internal schema defines how) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 543.10 Td (data is stored physically, for example in which files and with which indexes. The conceptual schema) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 528.81 Td (describes the logical structure of the whole database: entities, attributes and relationships. External) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 514.52 Td (schemas define the views that individual user groups or applications see.) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 491.66 Td (Mappings connect the levels. A query against an external view is translated into a query against the) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 477.38 Td (conceptual schema and then into operations on the internal level. Because each level only depends on) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 463.09 Td (the mapping to the next one, changes on one level can often be hidden from the levels above.) Tj ET
BT /Ff5d2de5f3a71699ae4b2d83179e62d09e6fc4126 13.00 Tf ET
BT 56.69 428.89 Td (1.3 Data Independence) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 406.22 Td (Physical data independence means that the internal schema can change, for example by adding an) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 391.93 Td (index or moving data to another disk, without changing the conceptual schema or the applications.) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 377.64 Td (Logical data independence means that the conceptual schema can be extended, for example by a new) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 363.36 Td (attribute, without changing external views that do not use it.) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 340.50 Td (Data independence is the main reason why database applications survive decades of changes in) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 326.21 Td (hardware and storage technology. It is also why query languages are declarative: an application states) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 311.92 Td (which data it needs, not how the DBMS should find it.) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 8.00 Tf ET
BT 56.69 34.02 Td (Database Systems - Lecture Notes · Seite 3 von 9) Tj ET

