BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 8.00 Tf ET
BT /Ff5d2de5f3a71699ae4b2d83179e62d09e6fc4126 18.00 Tf ET
BT 56.69 779.53 Td (2 The Relational Model and SQL) Tj ET
BT /Ff5d2de5f3a71699ae4b2d83179e62d09e6fc4126 13.00 Tf ET
BT 56.69 745.51 Td (2.1 Relations and Keys) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 722.83 Td (In the relational model, data is stored in relations, which are sets of tuples over a fixed list of attributes.) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 708.55 Td (Each attribute has a domain of atomic values. A relation schema consists of the relation name and its) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 694.26 Td (attributes; the relation itself is the current set of tuples.) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 671.40 Td (A superkey is a set of attributes whose values identify each tuple uniquely. A candidate key is a minimal) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 657.12 Td (superkey, and one candidate key is chosen as the primary key. A foreign key is a set of attributes that) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 642.83 Td (refers to the primary key of another relation; referential integrity requires that every foreign key value) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 628.54 Td (exists in the referenced relation.) Tj ET
BT /Ff5d2de5f3a71699ae4b2d83179e62d09e6fc4126 13.00 Tf ET
BT 56.69 594.35 Td (2.2 Relational Algebra) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 571.67 Td (Relational algebra provides operators that take relations as input and produce relations as output.) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 557.38 Td (Selection chooses tuples that satisfy a condition, projection keeps a subset of attributes, and the) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 543.10 Td (Cartesian product combines every tuple of one relation with every tuple of another. Union and) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 528.81 Td (difference work on relations with the same schema, and renaming changes attribute names.) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 505.95 Td (The join combines tuples of two relations that agree on given attributes; it can be expressed as a) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 491.66 Td (product followed by a selection. Because every operator returns a relation, expressions can be nested) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 477.38 Td (arbitrarily, which is the basis for query optimization: equivalent expressions can be evaluated at very) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 463.09 Td (different costs.) Tj ET
BT /Ff5d2de5f3a71699ae4b2d83179e62d09e6fc4126 13.00 Tf ET
BT 56.69 428.89 Td (2.3 Queries in SQL) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 406.22 Td (SQL is the standard query language of relational systems. A query has the basic form SELECT) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 391.93 Td (attributes FROM relations WHERE condition. Joins can be written as conditions in the WHERE clause) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 377.64 Td (or with the JOIN keyword. GROUP BY partitions the result into groups, and aggregate functions such) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 363.36 Td (as COUNT, SUM and AVG compute one value per group.) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 340.50 Td (Subqueries may appear in the WHERE clause, for example with IN or EXISTS. ORDER BY sorts the) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 326.21 Td (result. Unlike relational algebra, SQL works with multisets: duplicates are kept unless DISTINCT is) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 311.92 Td (specified.) Tj ET
BT /Ff5d2de5f3a71699ae4b2d83179e62d09e6fc4126 13.00 Tf ET
BT 56.69 277.73 Td (2.4 Normal Forms) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 255.05 Td (Normalization avoids redundancy and the update anomalies it causes. A relation is in first normal form) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 240.76 Td (if all attribute values are atomic. It is in second normal form if, in addition, no non-key attribute depends) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 226.48 Td (on only part of a candidate key. Third normal form also excludes transitive dependencies of non-key) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 212.19 Td (attributes on a key.) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 189.33 Td (Boyce-Codd normal form requires that the left side of every non-trivial functional dependency is a) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 175.05 Td (superkey. Decomposition into third normal form is always possible without losing information or) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 10.50 Tf ET
BT 56.69 160.76 Td (dependencies; for Boyce-Codd normal form, preserving all dependencies is not always possible.) Tj ET
BT /F0a76705d18e0494dd24cb573e53aa0a8c710ec99 8.00 Tf ET
BT 56.69 34.02 Td (Database Systems - Lecture Notes · Seite 4 von 9) Tj ET

